PLAIN-SPEAK PREREGISTERED QUESTION

We have tested the organs.

Now we test the organism.

A real Yggdrasil-like system cannot use one mechanism at a time.

The same population has to:

get damaged;
repair;
decide what healthy means;
adapt without losing identity;
change jobs;
put cells to sleep;
replace witnesses;
wake cells back up;
remember where it came from;
split during communication failure;
merge again;
and keep doing this repeatedly.

The danger is that two individually safe mechanisms may hand authority to each other in an unsafe order.

05AC deliberately tests those handoffs.

If 05AC is positive,
we will have moved beyond:

"this repair mechanism works"

or

"this hibernation mechanism works."

We will have evidence that the closed mechanisms can coexist
inside one persistent developmental control loop.

That is the threshold for beginning a separate first application prototype track.

It would still not mean Yggdrasil is production ready.

It would mean the research architecture is coherent enough to stop adding isolated mechanisms
and attempt one useful persistent synthetic organism.

